<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine has $798 mln Q2 current a/c deficit.</title>
<headline>Ukraine has $798 mln Q2 current a/c deficit.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine posted a current account deficit of $798 million in second quarter 1996, down from a $980 million first quarter shortfall, a central bank statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>The bank issued the following balance of payment details.</p>
<p> UKRAINE BALANCE OF PAYMENTS (in $mln)  Q2		 Q1</p>
<p> Current account balance		   -798	     -980</p>
<p> Balance on trade and services	    -22	     -560</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves		 +216	     -361</p>
<p> Direct investments			   +80	     +115</p>
<p> Portfolio investments			+11		 +9</p>
<p> Foreign credits (from IMF)		+291		  0</p>
<p>NOTE - 1996 is the first year the central bank has calculated the above figures.</p>
<p>--Natalia Zinets, Kiev Newsroom +380 44 229 2264</p>
</text>
